From: Hongjian Zhang <hongjian.zhang@gl-inet.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Nov 2026 15:34:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: rtl8366ub: sync tagger with PR #24237 head 1713e8be63

Replace the stale 95-line tagger with the current 268-line upstream
tagger. The old tagger cannot decode trapped control frames at all, so
0004's BPDU/IGMP/MLD traps (driver side) delivered frames that the
tagger dropped as "received untagged frame" - breaking STP and bridge
multicast snooping. The upstream tagger adds:

- native Realtek control-tag TX/RX (ETH_P_REALTEK 8-byte tag), pairing
  with 0004's INSERT_TRAPPED cpu-tag mode; ordinary data frames keep
  the plain 802.1Q business VLAN so PPE offload still parses them
- skb_set_mac_header() fix for trapped frames
- per-port control-frame egress (KEEP + LEARN_DIS, respects STP states)
- VLAN-aware bridge egress classification (business VID, PVID fallback)

Also add the factory-data nvmem cells (ddns/sn-bak/sn/country-code,
offsets verified against GL stock firmware by dmtpascoal, matching the
MT2500 layout in main) and align the chosen-node property order, making
the board DTS byte-identical with PR #24237 head 1713e8be63 (2026-11-05,
restructured into four commits).

Not ported from that revision: the 795-11 special-tag gating split (0001
already carries the same semantics inline; this baseline lacks the
mtk_uses_dsa() helper), the 999-90 PPE-offload redesign (0003 covers the
same RTL8366UB policy; replace 0003 with the upstream form at the next
baseline bump) and the 6.18.56+ dummy-dev removal (needed on 6.18.52).

Adapted-by: Kitsune <km2077@foxmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Hongjian Zhang <hongjian.zhang@gl-inet.com>
---
